evention of antimicrobial resistance in hospitals</article-title><source>Clin Infect Dis</source><year>1997</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>584</fpage><lpage>599</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9314444</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Falagas</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Karveli</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>World Wide Web resources of antimicrobial resistance</article-title><source>Clin Infect Dis</source><year>2006</year><volume>43</volume><fpage>630</fpage><lpage>633</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16886158</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/506443</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Centers for Disease Control and Prevention</collab></person-group><article-title>Infection control in health care settings</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cdc.gov/ncidod/dhqp/index.html"/></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eysenbach</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Citation advantage of open access articles</article-title><source>PLoS Biol</source><year>2006</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>e157</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16683865</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pbio.0040157</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>